     array['herb', 'edible', 'medicinal', 'fragrant', 'pet-safe'], false),
    ('Pudina (Mint)', 'Mentha spicata', 'herbs-greens',
     'Fresh mint for borhani, chutney and lemonade.',
     E'Grows like a weed — in a good way. Keep it in its own pot so it doesn''t take over.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Bright light with afternoon shade\n- Keep the soil moist\n- Cut back hard when it gets leggy\n\n**Good to know:** not recommended around cats and dogs.',
     90, null, 62, 10, 'mint', 'medium', 'easy', 1, 30, false, false, true, 30,
     array['herb', 'edible', 'kitchen', 'beginner', 'fast-growing'], false),
    ('Dhonepata (Coriander)', 'Coriandrum sativum', 'herbs-greens',
     'A pot of fresh coriander leaves for every dal and curry.',
     E'Best in the cooler months. Sow a new pot every three weeks for a continuous supply.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun in winter, part shade in summer\n- Keep the soil lightly moist\n- Harvest outer leaves first',
     60, null, 70, 12, 'coriander', 'full_sun', 'easy', 2, 21, true, false, true, 30,
     array['herb', 'edible', 'kitchen', 'winter', 'pet-safe'], false),
    ('Lemongrass', 'Cymbopogon citratus', 'herbs-greens',
     'Citrus-scented stalks for tea, Thai curries and soups.',
     E'A tough, clumping grass that loves sun and water. Cut a few stalks at the base whenever you need them.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun\n- Water regularly\n- Divide the clump every year',
     150, null, 33, 6, 'lemongrass', 'full_sun', 'easy', 2, 30, false, false, true, 90,
     array['herb', 'edible', 'tea', 'fragrant'], false),
    ('Kari Pata (Curry Leaf)', 'Murraya koenigii', 'herbs-greens',
     'Aromatic curry leaves straight from the plant to the tadka.',
     E'Fresh curry leaves have a flavour dried ones never match. A slow starter that grows into a generous shrub.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun\n- Water when the topsoil is dry\n- Pinch tips to encourage branching',
     220, null, 24, 5, 'curry-leaf', 'full_sun', 'easy', 3, 30, false, false, true, 150,
     array['herb', 'edible', 'kitchen', 'aromatic'], false),
    ('Stevia', 'Stevia rebaudiana', 'herbs-greens',
     'The sweet-leaf plant — a natural sugar alternative for tea.',
     E'A single leaf sweetens a cup of tea. Harvest before flowering for the sweetest leaves.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun\n- Keep the soil lightly moist\n- Pinch flower buds as they appear',
     180, null, 21, 5, 'stevia', 'full_sun', 'moderate', 2, 30, true, false, true, 50,
     array['herb', 'edible', 'sweetener', 'pet-safe'], false),
    ('Rosemary', 'Salvia rosmarinus', 'herbs-greens',
     'Pine-scented needles for roasts and breads.',
     E'Hates wet feet, so use a gritty mix and a terracotta pot. Protect from heavy monsoon rain.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun\n- Let the soil dry between waterings\n- Snip sprigs often to keep it bushy',
     280, null, 0, 5, 'rosemary', 'full_sun', 'moderate', 5, 60, true, false, true, 60,
     array['herb', 'edible', 'fragrant', 'mediterranean', 'pet-safe'], false),
    ('Pui Shak (Malabar Spinach)', 'Basella alba', 'herbs-greens',
     'A climbing spinach with thick, juicy leaves that loves the heat.',
     E'When regular spinach bolts in the heat, pui shak thrives. Cook the leaves and tender stems like spinach.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun\n- Water daily in summer\n- Give it a small trellis',
     70, null, 45, 10, 'pui-shak', 'full_sun', 'easy', 1, 14, false, false, true, 300,
     array['greens', 'edible', 'climber', 'summer'], false),
    ('Kolmi Shak (Water Spinach)', 'Ipomoea aquatica', 'herbs-greens',
     'Fast, tender greens that regrow after every cutting.',
     E'Grows in soil or a shallow tub of water. Cut it back to 10 cm and it regrows within a fortnight.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun\n- Keep the soil wet\n- Harvest often',
     60, null, 52, 10, 'kolmi-shak', 'full_sun', 'easy', 1, 14, false, false, true, 30,
     array['greens', 'edible', 'fast-growing', 'regrows'], false),
    ('Lal Shak (Red Amaranth)', 'Amaranthus tricolor', 'herbs-greens',
     'Crimson-leaved greens ready to harvest in four weeks.',
     E'A colourful, nutritious leafy green that grows quickly from seedlings. Stir-fry with garlic for a classic side.\n\n**Care tips**\n- Full sun\n- Keep the soil moist\n- Harvest by cutting the whole plant or picking leaves',
     60, null, 58, 10, 'lal-shak', 'full_sun', 'easy', 1, 14, false, false, true, 40,
